## 6. Preferred Patterns

### 6.1 Flutter Patterns

| Pattern | Usage |
|---|---|
| **BLoC** | Primary state management. Event-driven, unidirectional data flow. |
| **Repository Pattern** | Abstract interface → concrete impl. Decouples BLoC from data source. |
| **Either / Functional Error Handling** | Custom `Either<Failure, T>` with `fold()`. No exceptions in BLoC layer. |
| **Service Locator (GetIt)** | Single registration point. Singletons for auth BLoC & socket. Factories for feature BLoCs. |
| **GoRouter redirect** | Centralized auth guard with role-based routing (admin vs user). |
| **Socket Lifecycle Manager** | Widget wrapping entire app tree for socket connect/disconnect based on auth state. |
| **Part files** | Socket handlers split via Dart `part`/`part of` for organization. |

### 6.2 Backend Patterns

| Pattern | Usage |
|---|---|
| **MVC + Service Layer** | Route → Controller (thin) → Service (logic) → Model |
| **RBAC middleware** | Role-based access with permission arrays per role |
| **JWT dual-token** | Access token (short-lived) + Refresh token (stored in DB) |
| **OTP with TTL index** | MongoDB TTL auto-deletes unverified signup users after 10 min |
| **Socket rooms** | User rooms (1:1 notifications), admin_room (broadcast), listening_room (collaboration) |
| **Zod validation** | Input validation using Zod schemas in services |

---

## 7. API Convention

- **Base path**: `/api/{resource}`
- **Auth endpoints**: `/api/auth/login`, `/api/auth/register`, `/api/auth/refresh`, etc.
- **CRUD resources**: `/api/{resource}` (GET list), `/api/{resource}/:id` (GET detail), POST/PUT/DELETE
- **Admin endpoints**: `/api/{resource}/admin/list`, `/api/{resource}/admin/:id`
- **Pagination response**: `{ data: [...], pagination: { page, limit, totalDocs, totalPages, hasNextPage } }`
- **Error response**: `{ message: "Human-readable error" }`

